    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Chalcolithic phase represents the first stage in human history where metal (copper) was used along with stone tools.",
        "Prominent regional cultures include Ahar-Banas culture (Rajasthan), Malwa culture (Madhya Pradesh), and Jorwe culture (Maharashtra).",
        "Wheel-made Black and Red Ware (BRW) decorated with white geometric patterns was the predominant pottery style.",
        "Agriculture and pastoralism formed the economic backbone, cultivating wheat, barley, rice, and lentils."
      ],
